blitzy-nav-toggle:
Accessible name of the control that reveals the site navigation inside the floating navigation card on viewports narrower than 768px, where that navigation collapses into a disclosure. The disclosure is built from CSS alone, so it keeps working when JavaScript is unavailable. One control both opens and closes the menu, which means the label never changes and the translation has to stay state-neutral: do not word it as "Close navigation menu" or otherwise claim whether the menu is open. This message takes no parameters.

See also:
* {{msg-mw|Navigation-heading}}

blitzy-personal-toggle:
Accessible name of the control inside the floating navigation card that reveals the user menu, the disclosure listing the personal tools MediaWiki provides for whoever is reading. The disclosure is built from CSS alone, so it keeps working when JavaScript is unavailable. One control both opens and closes the menu, so the translation has to stay state-neutral: do not word it as "Close user menu" or add anything that asserts the current state. This message takes no parameters.

See also:
* {{msg-mw|Personaltools}}

blitzy-toc-toggle:
Accessible name of the control that reveals the table of contents where that list is rendered inline, on viewports narrower than 1024px; wider viewports present the same list as a sticky sidebar card and show no such control. The disclosure is built from CSS alone, so it keeps working when JavaScript is unavailable. One control both opens and closes the list, so the translation has to stay state-neutral: do not word it as "Hide table of contents". This message takes no parameters.

See also:
* {{msg-mw|Toc}}
